Re-review request for PR #31 at its new head on origin/v1/plan-10-qual-host-2; fetch first. It adds two things:

**(1) The asUser narrowing** in eval/validate.mjs: `/usr/bin/sudo -n -u <user> -- <absolute cmd>`, with no `env -i`. Call sites are updated in run.mjs and eval/host/validate.mjs, and the test is in cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts.

**(2) Fixes for your last 7 findings:**
- stale pending dirs are pruned and never adopt anything;
- the runtime purge needs both a confirmed ledger entry and the `.nexus-qual-managed` marker;
- a dangling symlink at the sudoers or unit path is a collision, and nothing is written through a link (`rm -f` before writing the unit);
- files are recorded with their sha256 and removed only if unchanged (record_file uses exact awk ENVIRON matching, because the unit path contains a backslash);
- dirs that couldn't be removed stay in the ledger;
- an interrupted useradd gets an explicit recovery message;
- the ledger dir is removed after a full rollback.

Results: the container test is 23/23 PASS (you may re-run it); eval_integrity + eval_harness are 34/34 locally.

Also, please confirm the fixes on **PR #30** at 6b33a1a, relative to your review of 8cbb7eb. The command baseline now runs on a throwaway copy of the staged workspace. A timeout, overflow or containment failure there is a harness error; only a normal exit counts. Baseline resources are recorded as resources.t3Baseline.

Verdict per PR, under 300 words.

